  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "P1",
      "hash": "8efebe0b6a659108b0fa5ddc98b0dc51e506913a67e4e2ae589202761298a28c",
      "heading": "Lead",
      "excerpt": "Çatalhöyük (English: Chatalhoyuk; /ˌtʃɑːtɑːlˈhuːjʊk/, cha-tal-HOO-yuhk; Turkish pronunciation: [tʃaˈtaɫhœjyc]; also Çatal Höyük and Çatal Hü",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "hash": "3e1d1d816290d29ffac6f48268ffc1de7cb6b689f8295ba0d5222bdc534f9f0a",
      "heading": "Archaeology",
      "excerpt": "The site was discovered by James Mellaart in 1958 during a regional survey of the Konya Plain. He led a team which excavated there for four ",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "hash": "84a4ca7cb9a0e7bf811077a8a31f898b08fda30fc5dc37673521d70e089e3d49",
      "heading": "Archaeology",
      "excerpt": "Mellaart was banned from Turkey for his involvement in the Dorak affair, in which he published drawings of supposedly important Bronze Age a",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "hash": "df328e10d3a561f537751b10a31589e71f6b418d306fdeef04f631c72a830341",
      "heading": "Archaeology",
      "excerpt": "At the Western Mound, upon which Mellaart had only opened two trenches, in 1961, Jonathan Last and Catriona Gibson excavated in 1998. In 200",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "hash": "8d108c60414df29facbaf1dec517e8a8f83cd29a3cddc8911404241b069ec2ec",
      "heading": "Archaeology",
      "excerpt": "In August 2025, archaeologists led by Arkadiusz Marciniak of Poznań University revealed a mortuary structure referred to as the \"House of th",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "hash": "3ccc075cd5626ba1d0612aaf284b0bf99417b67b3ed2cf4f62604f11228abf8e",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "Çatalhöyük was composed entirely of domestic buildings with no obvious public buildings. While some of the larger rooms have rather ornate m",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "hash": "3d2a1882d6e6772ded1bd0dd1e05b9c1b83de88cce587c92573aeaddbe53c515",
      "heading": "Religion",
      "excerpt": "A feature of Çatalhöyük are its female figurines. Mellaart, the original excavator, argued that these carefully made figurines, carved and m",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "hash": "724511a1c7fc5d899ce151fbd9542200841e2cbde8d856970b6034bdab265ab3",
      "heading": "Organization",
      "excerpt": "Çatalhöyük has strong evidence of an egalitarian society, as no houses with distinctive features (belonging to royalty or religious hierarch",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "hash": "b34a01a2a84b60875c6f3cf327b96ba2bd71b503a8d989472e9b82481dd77301",
      "heading": "Agriculture",
      "excerpt": "In the upper levels of the site, it becomes apparent that the people of Çatalhöyük were honing skills in agriculture and the domestication o",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "hash": "be5f23a5dfc76c1e89087af0ec9b04ef9bdae8f45d160d1a9a74acfa7c19c326",
      "heading": "Museum",
      "excerpt": "In 2023, an information and visitor centre developed by Konya Metropolitan Municipality opened at the site. Its exhibition halls feature int",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "hash": "cef2897c14b8da7f7c4039b9f5ee2578a7ab0c699b8dd444897f3e501e09514c",
      "heading": "Archaeology",
      "excerpt": "Finds at the site, from the Neolithic layers, included a number of textiles which are rarely preserved in early sites. Most were found in a ",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "hash": "54c7d7a9eef3bbb8ea6953f325ec285debfcaa732840833fec8e5ab6e08ebf14",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "Initial estimates suggested an average population of between 5,000 and 7,000. However, more recent work using revised ideas of the distribut",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "hash": "9e09c7d571ec8b8542d29a6592ed9f69fd8c941fa51ef31fcc7c6e0394053ba6",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "The sites were set up as large numbers of buildings clustered together. Households looked to their neighbours for help, trade, and possible ",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P14",
      "hash": "675f3f667168e268e61d14e02b00fd487349024536c89d3675f675d6a17fb284",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "Houses had plaster interiors accessed by squared-off timber ladders or steep stairs. These were usually on the south wall of the room, as we",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P15",
      "hash": "d4b51c270fe1e9de263336f8ae7dc622ad45078a3a8793373e9eef67d1a91f46",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "All rooms were kept scrupulously clean. Archaeologists identified very little rubbish in the buildings, finding middens outside the ruins, w",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    },
    {
      "id": "P16",
      "hash": "970568f6bfd9d8d00a18bbfe1a04934c0c98698f008923a8cc88e15c40fb7eac",
      "heading": "Culture",
      "excerpt": "As a part of ritual life, the people of Çatalhöyük buried their dead within the village. Human remains have been found in pits beneath the f",
      "revisionUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379818880"
    }
  ],
